A||N||10||2xsess||ECM Heatup||||5||
Z||000000||2xsess||10-02-2000||10:32 PM||||As I was driving back from Madrox86GT place I noticed that my back was getting warm. I put my hand in between the passenger side seat and the console, right by the comp vents and man was it warm. I was wondering if this is normal? <P>Thanks in advance for your help.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT<p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||10-02-2000||11:01 PM||||Maybe some small computer fans could be mounted in the enclosure to help ventilate the ECM better?<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||10-02-2000||11:07 PM||||I had the same thought. well you know what they say....GREAT MINDS....<P>Does anyone else have this problem?<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||14
Z||000003||theogre||10-02-2000||11:48 PM||||My 87 DIS 4 cyl ECM throws a bunch of heat. You really notice it if you open the storage box after the cars been run awhile. I thought about adding fans awhile back. If I could find one that was quiet I'd do it. Most of the plastic framed "boxer" fans used in computers are pretty noisy.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||10-02-2000||11:53 PM||||My '87's and '88 (4 BANGERS)do the same thing. I wonder if it's heat radiating from the converter to the interior?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||10-02-2000||11:57 PM||||The wiring harnesses and shift cables run through the firewall behind the console. If one (or more) of the seals for these have come out then hot air from the engine compartment can come in. I would check that first.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||10-03-2000||01:23 AM||||Assuming it is a problem with the ECM.. conventional electronics cooling techniques would work. bigger heatsinks on the chips, fans, etc..<P>the case fans I have in my system are pretty quiet.. wouldn't hear them at all in a Fiero, with the engine running.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000007||theogre||10-03-2000||09:18 AM||||Even if there are no air leaks from the engine bay, there is nothing realy to get rid of the ECM's own heat. If you look at how the grates are placed vs where the ECM sits there really isn't squat for convection path. It's a wonder the fool things don't melt.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tigger||10-03-2000||09:46 AM||||I like to use my storage box to heat small inanimate objects so they are nice and toasty after a long drive.<P>Works great to keep gloves warm in the winter.  Also I pop two slices of bread in there, close it up, drive off, and then enjoy two slices of toast by the time I reach my destination!  Now let's see a toaster oven feature in a Aztek, HUH  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">          <BR> <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000009||2xsess||10-03-2000||01:38 PM||||HHHMMMM...toast....could be used for pop-tarts too then, cool <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Well atleast now I know it is a common thing, Thank you all<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||6
Z||000010||286SE'S||10-03-2000||03:50 PM||||Put two 12 volt fans in series. Each will get 6 volts and run at half speed and be very quiet. I do this on my stereo equipment. It may be nothing to worry about. I saw a 2001 chevy truck at an auto show and the ECM was in the engine compartment right above the exhaust manifold! ||||reg||7
